"""Write the tl-04 close-out delegated-decision block to tmp/tl-04/dd_block.md (the shell then appends it ONCE with >>).
Run after build.py --write, post.py and verify_out.py:  python3 -I tmp/tl-04/dd.py
All figures are read from the written files."""
import os, json, sys
HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
ROOT = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(HERE, '..', '..'))
G = os.path.join(ROOT, 'docs', 'battle-theatre', 'GOVERNANCE')
cnt = json.load(open(os.path.join(G, 'horde', 'tl-04', 'counts.json'), encoding='utf-8'))
corr = [json.loads(l) for l in open(os.path.join(G, 'timeline_corrections', 'tl-04.jsonl'), encoding='utf-8')]
dp = os.path.join(G, 'decisions', 'DELEGATED-DECISIONS-2026-11-11.md')
txt = open(dp, encoding='utf-8').read()
if 'DD-TL04-01' in txt:
    print('decision block already present in the decisions file; nothing written')
    sys.exit(0)
tv = cnt['tier_vs_seed']
prom = ', '.join(tv['promotion']) or 'none'
dem = ', '.join(tv['demotion']) or 'none'
above_shard = [c['id'] for c in corr if c['tier_change']['note'].find('higher than the tier the shard audit') >= 0]
sc = ', '.join(cnt['rows_with_scenarios'])
dflt = ', '.join(c['id'] for c in corr if c.get('default'))
orc = [c for r in corr for c in r['citations'] if c['source_id'] == 'OR27']
n_or = len(orc)
n_diff = sum(1 for c in orc if c.get('page_running_head_model'))
n_img = sum(1 for c in orc if (c.get('scan') or {}).get('printed_page_read_on_image'))
leaves = set()
for c in orc:
    s = c.get('scan') or {}
    for k in ('leaf', 'leaf_end'):
        if s.get(k) is not None:
            leaves.add((c['part'], s[k]))
pages_changed = sorted({(r['id'], c['key']) for r in corr for c in r['citations'] if c.get('page_running_head_model') and c['source_id'] == 'OR27'})
block = '''

## Added 2026-11-16 by the timeline close-out of shard tl-04 (first pass 2026-11-13/14, second reading 2026-11-16; DELEGATED, reversible by the owner, not owner decisions; detail in horde/tl-04/REPORT.md and timeline_corrections/tl-04.jsonl)

| id | question | options | chosen default | evidence | tier | reversibility | product marking |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| DD-TL04-01 | Effective tier of the 58 rows of timeline shard tl-04 (T1-173 to T2-005) | keep the shard-audit tiers; apply the close-out tier of each corrected claim | Apply the tier in `corrected_claim.tier` of GOVERNANCE/timeline_corrections/tl-04.jsonl (field `tier_change` shows seed, shard-audit and corrected tier). Against the seed: promotions %s; demotions %s. Against the shard-audit tier: higher on %s. A promotion applies to the corrected wording only; every unsupported remainder keeps its own tier (open gap) and its proposed register entry (tl-04-CO-<row>.md). | every citation re-matched verbatim in the local Official Records, library and NPS texts (%d citations); promotions need a non-lead source that supports exactly the corrected claim (Law cl.4), met by the quotes stored in the line | as stated per row | seed rows and shard files are not edited; the overlay is the effective tier; the owner may revert any row | tier glyph on every sub-claim that is not documented |
| DD-TL04-02 | Source conflicts found in tl-04 with no recorded default | pick a default; carry every value | No default is picked. Every value stays a selectable scenario (rows with scenarios: %s). The only defaults named in the lines are RECORDED ones, applied unchanged: C-001 (T1-221), C-002 (T1-222), C-004 (T1-199), C-027 (T1-217), C-038 (T2-003), C-039 (T1-175, T2-001) and DD-F2-07 of shard fence-2 (T1-182, T1-200, T1-201); rows that carry a `default`: %s. Where this close-out found evidence that bears on a recorded default (C-027: the night of Jul 2 at Taneytown, Buford p.928 and Devin p.939), the evidence is carried as a scenario beside the default and the default is not changed here. | timeline_corrections/tl-04.jsonl `scenarios` and `default` | documented (each value carries its source tier) | scenario switch | scenario selector with source and tier per value |
| DD-TL04-03 | Which sources count as non-lead for a documented sub-claim in shard tl-04 | Official Records only; Official Records plus eyewitness and contemporary texts plus official-body reports; every secondary page | The Official Records; eyewitness and contemporary texts of the library (Jacobs 1864, Everett 1863, Haskell written 1863, Early 1877 in the Southern Historical Society Papers, Longstreet 1896, the article of Brevet Maj. Gen. Hunt, chief of artillery, in Battles and Leaders vol. 3 pp.255-284); National Park Service reports and articles for what they literally say (marked as a government report that names no primary source). Wikipedia, Stone Sentinels, HistoryNet, Strategypage, Gettysburg Daily and other secondary pages named in the seed stay leads and carry no documented sub-claim. | GOVERNANCE/horde/tl-04/REPORT.md | documented (class stated per citation: `source_class`, `witness`) | restrict to the Official Records | source class shown with each citation |
| DD-TL04-04 | Jacobs's weather readings (Jul 1-2: sky, 72/76/74 and 74/81/76, cirro-stratus at 9 p.m.) | show as documented; show as second-hand | Shown as inferred, marked second-hand: they reach the project through an 1885 article and typed transcriptions; the original observation forms were not read | data-src/environment/weather_by_day.json (verification_summary); timeline_corrections/tl-04.jsonl rows T1-189, 190, 195, 219, 225 | inferred | promote when the original form or the 1885 issue is read | tier glyph and the word second-hand |
| DD-TL04-05 | Plan text of T1-220: illumination 'falls from 99 to 93 percent' | keep the plan text; show the computed values | Show the computed values (99.0 percent at moonrise 19:53, 98.6 at midnight, 97.7 at moonset 06:14 LMT); the plan's 93 percent is recorded as contradicted by two independent computations; correcting the plan text is left to the owner or integrator | horde/tl-04/astro_check.json (PyEphem 4.2.1) and the repository ephemeris | inferred (computed) | restore the plan value | computed value with its method |
| DD-TL04-06 | Printed page of an Official Records citation in tl-04 (the running-head page model of tools/bt/or27_pages.py against the page of the scan leaf) | running-head model; page of the scan leaf | The page of the scan leaf first (archive.org page index aligned to the OCR text, tools/bt/kit_or27_leafmap.py), the same rule as the tl-02 close-out. Of %d Official Records citations %d differ from the running-head model (or were interpolated there; each carries `page_running_head_model`); the printed number was confirmed on the page image (second OCR of the scan, or looked at) for %d citations on %d leaves. Example: Doles, OR27-2-R514, is printed p.582 and not p.581. | timeline_corrections/tl-04.jsonl fields `printed_page`, `page_basis`, `scan`, `page_running_head_model`; tmp/tl-04/scan/ocr; scans tmp/kit-plan/or27-pdf (read-only) | documented | restore the running-head pages | page shown as printed |
| DD-TL04-07 | An Official Records digit that the OCR text prints differently from the page image (Greene, OR27-1-R307, p.856: the text reads '13 o'clock', the image '12 o'clock'; found in the second reading and read on the page image: Geary, R293 p.825, 'about 2 p. m.' where the text reads 3 p. m.; Wright, R224 p.665, 'from 32 to 35 miles' where the text reads 33; Rodes, R506 p.555, 'a loss of 2,500 men' where the text reads 3,600) | store the OCR text as the quote and say so; store the image reading as the quote | The quote stays the OCR text (it is what the tools can re-match); the image reading is carried in the citation field `reading` and in a note, and the sub-claim and the corrected claim state the image reading (the hour of Geary's advance moves from 15:00 to 14:00 in T1-176 and T2-005, the march of the VI Corps is 32 to 35 miles in T1-191, Rodes' loss is 2,500 in T1-186). Consistent with the reading of shard fence-2 (DD-F2-07). | tmp/tl-04/scan/img (page image of PDF page 880 of cu31924077699761.pdf, viewed) | documented | edit the row data and rebuild | the claim shows the hour read on the page image |
| DD-TL04-08 | Which texts that were local after the first pass count as sources for a documented sub-claim in shard tl-04, and at which tier | every text counts as documented; documented only for 1863 sources; later books at a lower tier | The 1863 report of the U.S. Sanitary Commission (J. H. Douglas, signed Aug. 15, 1863, with the statements of its representatives) is documented as what it says; the 1864 letters of a relief worker (E. B. S., second-hand where they relay residents) are documented as what they say and marked second-hand; later books (Hoke 1887, the county history of 1886, Reily 1885, Barton 1898) support a sub-claim only at tier inferred (the rule of DD-TL01-11); pages of 1863 newspapers (Library of Congress, Chronicling America) are contemporary statements of what the paper prints, one text printed in several papers counts once, and the OCR text is quoted as it stands (a reading from a page image is carried in the field `reading` only where an image was read); Wikipedia, Stone Sentinels, HistoryNet and the other secondary pages named in the seed stay leads | horde/tl-04/REPORT.md; ext_lib.py (source ids) | documented or inferred (stated per citation: `source_class`, `witness`) | restrict to the earlier classes of DD-TL04-03 | source class shown with each citation |
| DD-TL04-09 | T2-003 (Spangler farm hospital): effect of the Sanitary Commission report on the recorded default C-038 | change C-038; leave it unchanged | Unchanged: range 1,000-2,000, all five values listed, no headline number. The report of Aug. 15, 1863 (p.24) gives the Eleventh Corps hospital at the house and farm of Geo. Spangler 1,900 wounded (1,800 Union and 100 Confederate), 'approximative only' and undated, so two of the five values (1,800 and 1,900) now have a source and the row moves from gap to partially_supported; whether the status note of C-038 ('No primary or institutional count found') is updated, and whether the default narrows, is left to the owner or integrator (request note) | timeline_corrections/tl-04.jsonl line T2-003, citations ussc_spang and ussc_table | documented for 1,800 and 1,900; open gap for the other values | restore the earlier wording of the row | counts as a range with every value; sourced values marked as approximate |
| DD-TL04-10 | The recipient of Hancock's dispatch of 5.25 p.m. (T1-175, T2-004) | keep the name Butterfield of the first close-out; say what the text prints | Say what the text prints: the dispatch is headed 'General:' with no addressee in the text read, and Hancock's report calls it a communication to the major-general commanding, sent by Captain Parker of his staff; the name Butterfield had no passage (Law cl.4) | OR27-1-R076 pp.366 and 368 | documented | restore the name if a passage is found | the unit field shows the addressee as the major-general commanding |
''' % (prom, dem, ', '.join(above_shard) or 'none', cnt['citations'], sc, dflt, n_or, n_diff, n_img, len(leaves))
open(os.path.join(HERE, 'dd_block.md'), 'w', encoding='utf-8', newline='\n').write(block)
print('decision block written to tmp/tl-04/dd_block.md; append ONCE with: cat tmp/tl-04/dd_block.md >> docs/battle-theatre/GOVERNANCE/decisions/DELEGATED-DECISIONS-2026-11-11.md')
